  "notes": [
    "Me gusta works like \"it pleases me\": the thing liked is the subject. With a plural thing it is me gustan: me gustan las arepas.",
    "After gustar, Spanish keeps el / la: me gusta el café, never me gusta café.",
    "Me encanta (\"it delights me\") is stronger than me gusta, and very common.",
    "A mí también agrees with a gustar sentence. After an ordinary verb it is yo también."
  ]
